A16_SMSS_72_M016936_034                                                       
                                                                              
Apollo 16 Soil Mechanics                                                      
Lunar Self-Recording Penetrometer (LSRP) Page C-1                             
                                                                              
Load Calibration Plot                                                         
                                                                              
This handdrawn plot shows the results the post-flight calibrations of         
the Lunar Self-Recording Penetrometer (LSRP) and comparison with the          
preflight calibration.  The plot gives the drum circumferential               
deflection (abscissa) from 0 to 15 millimeters versus the load                
(ordinate) from 0 to 200 Newtons.  The plot has a line representing the       
preflight calibrations produced from 12 tests, a line representing the        
postflight results before the lunar dust was cleaned off the LSRP using       
index setting 19 labelled postflight #19, and a line representing the         
postflight results using index 21 after the LSRP was washed off with          
alcohol, labelled postflight #21. There is a point at the top right           
labelled "maverick point #21" which was not used in creating the lines        
but is mentioned as a "special pt" in A16_SMSS_72_M016936_036, page C-3       
and A16_SMSS_72_M016936_038, page C-5.                                        
